referenceSolutions.java:
class Solution {
  public int[] bookingRackPositiveProofStrip(int[][] drawers, int k) {
    int[][] a=drawers; List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>();
    {int[][]rows=a.clone();Arrays.sort(rows,Comparator.comparingInt((int[]r)->r[1]).thenComparingInt(r->r[0]));int end=Integer.MIN_VALUE;for(int[]r:rows)if(r[0]>=end){out.add(r[1]-r[0]);end=r[1];}}
    return out.stream().filter(x->x>0).mapToInt(Integer::intValue).toArray();
  }
}

privateData.editorialMd:
The working idea

Each booking is [start,end] with start < end and occupies [start,end). Sort by end then start ascending; accept a booking if it starts at or after the last accepted end. Produce accepted durations in acceptance order. Negative times are allowed.

Return only the strictly positive values in the derived sequence, preserving their relative order and duplicates.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(n log n); space O(n).

